<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Auxois</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Auxois is a hilly farming region in the north-west of the Côte-d'Or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, whose chief town is Semur-en-Auxois. Its name derives from Alesia, the Gallic stronghold on Mont Auxois. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it formed one of the bailiwicks of the Duchy of Burgundy, and it is known today for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> rearing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/auxois.jpg" alt="Auxois" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cjp24 crop by Peli · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horse_and_hay_bale,_Auxois_horse,_Burgundy,_France._flip-crop2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
